<% page_title "Data" %>
<% content_for :description, "The registry and the change record as files, for anyone who wants to cite, chart or build on them. CSV, JSON and Atom, under ODC-By 1.0." %>
<% content_for :head, json_ld(
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  name: "Trained On: the registry and the change record",
  description: "Is this AI training on my prompts? What each tool's own terms say, quoted and dated, and every time the answer changed.",
  url: data_url,
  license: "https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/by/1-0/",
  isAccessibleForFree: true,
  creator: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Trained On", url: root_url },
  isBasedOn: "https://github.com/OpenTermsArchive/genai-contrib-versions",
  keywords: [ "AI training", "terms of service", "privacy policy", "generative AI", "prompts" ],
  dateModified: @last_capture&.to_date&.iso8601,
  distribution: [
    { "@type": "DataDownload", name: "registry.csv", encodingFormat: "text/csv", contentUrl: registry_csv_url },
    { "@type": "DataDownload", name: "changes.csv", encodingFormat: "text/csv", contentUrl: changes_csv_url },
    { "@type": "DataDownload", name: "vendors.json", encodingFormat: "application/json", contentUrl: api_v1_vendors_url },
    { "@type": "DataDownload", name: "changes.json", encodingFormat: "application/json", contentUrl: api_v1_changes_url }
  ]
) %>
<div class="prose">
<h1>Data</h1>
<p class="lede">The registry and the change record as files, for anyone who wants to cite, chart or build on them.</p>
<ul>
  <li><%= link_to "registry.csv", registry_csv_path %>: one row per vendor plan, with answer, quote, document, dates and source link.</li>
  <li><%= link_to "changes.csv", changes_csv_path %>: every published change, with classification, summary and the Open Terms Archive capture.</li>
  <li><%= link_to "/api/v1/vendors", api_v1_vendors_path %> and <%= link_to "/api/v1/changes", api_v1_changes_path %>: the same as JSON.</li>
  <li><%= link_to "changes.atom", changes_feed_path %>: a feed of published changes. Each vendor page has its own feed too.</li>
</ul>
<p>Licence: <a href="https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/by/1-0/">ODC-By 1.0</a>. Attribute "Trained On, derived from Open Terms Archive contributors".</p>
<p>Only published changes and verified rows appear in these files. Nothing is included before a person has reviewed it.</p>
</div>
